WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.300
Aladdin killed Jasmine.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.550
In his efforts to impress the princess
and win her hand

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:08.300
in marriage, this lovable street
rat made one fatal error.

00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:10.216
This: No.

00:00:10.216 --> 00:00:12.300
Jasmine. No, it is not safe.

00:00:12.316 --> 00:00:13.616
Magic carpet ride?

00:00:13.616 --> 00:00:15.916
More like tragic carpet ride.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:17.250
Did you see what I did there?

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.250
I'm pretty proud of that one.

00:00:22.816 --> 00:00:23.966
Hello Internet!

00:00:23.966 --> 00:00:26.116
Welcome to Film Theory.

00:00:26.116 --> 00:00:28.183
You ain’t never had a channel like me.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.516
Unless, of course, you watch Game Theory
too, in which case yeah...

00:00:30.516 --> 00:00:32.600
they are largely the same.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.400
Cover different
IP I suppose... Or not actually. Woopsy.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.883
So anyway, Disney is not doing that
hot these days, huh?

00:00:37.916 --> 00:00:40.050
They've had flop after flop at the box
office.

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:42.600
Tentpole brands like Marvel
and Star Wars are struggling.

00:00:42.616 --> 00:00:45.883
Their back catalog has been tarnished
by an onslaught of low effort, live action

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:49.166
remakes and even the parks division is
sweating heavily due to lower attendance

00:00:49.166 --> 00:00:54.116
and the shut down of a $350 million hotel
merely a year after its opening.

00:00:54.116 --> 00:00:57.466
Really kind of makes you yearn for
the golden days of classic Disney, right?

00:00:57.466 --> 00:01:00.683
The Renaissance era
where every movie was a certified classic

00:01:00.683 --> 00:01:03.550
that would go on to shape the childhoods
for generations of kids.

00:01:03.566 --> 00:01:04.533
I'm talking about the OGs

00:01:04.533 --> 00:01:08.333
here: Lion King, Little Mermaid, Beauty
and the Beast, Aladdin, all the ones

00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:11.633
that have been bled dry for an extra
billion dollars at the box office.

00:01:11.633 --> 00:01:13.666
Their originals are revered for a reason.

00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:17.750
Beautiful animation, amazing songs,
timeless stories, traumatic nightmare fuel

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.666
that'll need years of therapy to process.

00:01:19.666 --> 00:01:21.350
Oh, I'm sorry. Did you miss that last one?

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.716
Blocked it out of your memory
and all that? Well, let me refresh you.

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:26.083
The Disney classics were rife for terror.

00:01:26.116 --> 00:01:28.516
There were the scary moments,
of course, like Mufasa's death,

00:01:28.516 --> 00:01:31.883
the wolf attacks in Beauty and the Beast,
Hercules literally withering to dust

00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:35.100
and Prince Eric’s ship burning with him
and his dogs lives on the line.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.650
Then, of course,
he had the disturbing themes

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.733
that could also scar you: Bell
having to teach an angry, violent man

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.833
how to love Belle falling for the beast
because of Stockholm Syndrome, Bell

00:01:42.866 --> 00:01:45.350
being ostracized by society
for being a smart woman.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.066
Honestly,
there's a lot in Beating the Beast.

00:01:47.066 --> 00:01:50.366
But that movie's far from alone,
Claude Frollo’s addiction to pain, Ariel

00:01:50.366 --> 00:01:51.900
given up her voice for a man that she met

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:55.100
once, Aladdin using an enslaved creature
to help him lie about his life

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:58.733
so he can trick a woman he's
met once into marrying him.

00:01:58.733 --> 00:02:02.250
But not only is Aladdin responsible
for shamelessly gaslighting Jasmine

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.850
throughout the majority of the movie, he's
also responsible for her murder.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.033
‘But she doesn't die in the movie’,
I hear you saying.

00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:09.900
And yeah,
while you're technically correct.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.966
His actions would have definitely
killed her.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.166
See, about halfway through the film,
Aladdin takes Jasmine on a magic carpet

00:02:15.166 --> 00:02:16.350
ride during what's probably

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:19.050
the film's most iconic musical number,
A Whole New World.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:22.066
And during this little romantic getaway,
the pair fly out of Agrabah to go visit

00:02:22.066 --> 00:02:22.916
the pyramids of Egypt,

00:02:22.916 --> 00:02:26.633
the Acropolis of Athens, Greece
and the Forbidden City of Beijing, China.

00:02:26.666 --> 00:02:29.183
Honestly,
it's a pretty great date, on paper.

00:02:29.183 --> 00:02:30.150
But when you actually stop

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:33.650
and think about what's going on here,
you realize one huge problem.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.616
They do all of this
in the span of a single night.

00:02:36.683 --> 00:02:37.800
I mean, is that possible?

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:38.300
And if it is,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.900
they must be traveling at speeds
that would rip human flesh off the bone.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:50.116
Really puts this joke
into a brand new context.

00:02:50.116 --> 00:02:51.750
Goodbye indeed, Genie.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.900
So we ran the numbers to see if Aladdin's
magic carpet ride would be a one way

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.900
trip to romance
or a whole new world of pain.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:01.016
Join me, friends,
as I make it crystal clear that now

00:03:01.016 --> 00:03:04.700
they're in a whole screwed world with you.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.466
Don't you dare close your eyes.

00:03:06.466 --> 00:03:09.800
So for us to figure out exactly how badly
Aladdin and Jasmine would have been

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.866
injured during their little romantic
jaunt across the historical world.

00:03:12.866 --> 00:03:14.900
I figure we should probably narrow down
the main ways

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.066
that we see this killing them.

00:03:16.066 --> 00:03:19.316
The big two, how high they're flying
and how fast they're flying.

00:03:19.316 --> 00:03:21.200
Let's start off with how high
they actually flew.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.433
We see Aladdin and Jasmine

00:03:22.433 --> 00:03:24.566
flying through clouds
at multiple points in the song,

00:03:24.566 --> 00:03:26.300
which set off
some alarm bells in my brain.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.950
Since, you know, humans aren't
technically supposed to be up that high.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:32.266
See, the higher up you go, the less dense
the air is and the lower

00:03:32.266 --> 00:03:33.266
the level of oxygen.

00:03:33.266 --> 00:03:34.283
When you get high enough, there

00:03:34.283 --> 00:03:37.283
literally isn't enough oxygen in the air
for you to survive.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:39.800
And that's without even mentioning
how cold it's going to be the further up

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:40.250
you go.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:43.733
So overall, not exactly looking that great
for our two little lovebirds.

00:03:43.733 --> 00:03:46.050
That said, would going up this high
straight up kill them?

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:49.216
To find out, I first decided to figure out
how high they actually got.

00:03:49.216 --> 00:03:52.100
And I did that by identifying the clouds
that they're flying through.

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:55.166
Given the shape and volume of the clouds
I figured that they had to be either

00:03:55.166 --> 00:03:58.550
cumulus or cumulonimbus,
given how fluffy and full they looked.

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:03.116
Now cumulus clouds are found up to 6,500
feet in the sky, while cumulonimbus clouds

00:04:03.116 --> 00:04:06.350
can reach as high as 20,000 feet,
much higher.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.116
So which altitude
are we talking about here?

00:04:08.116 --> 00:04:11.083
Well, given that we also see the carpet
fly through a flock of what appear

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.183
to be cranes during part of the song,
we can actually identify these clouds

00:04:14.183 --> 00:04:15.116
as cumulus,

00:04:15.116 --> 00:04:18.983
since cranes typically fly at an altitude
of roughly 6,000 to 7,000 feet.

00:04:18.983 --> 00:04:20.566
As such,
we're just going to call this altitude

00:04:20.566 --> 00:04:24.466
right here, about 6,500 feet
or 2,000 meters to keep things simple.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.000
So how cold would it be up there?

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.450
And would Aladdin and Jasmine have died
from some subfreezing temperatures?

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:30.316
Well, yeah.

00:04:30.316 --> 00:04:33.383
At about 6,500 feet,
the temperature is going to be about 35

00:04:33.383 --> 00:04:38.216
degrees Fahrenheit or just about 1 to 2
degrees Celsius, slightly above freezing.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.400
So it might be a bit nippy
for this couple,

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.466
especially Jasmine,
considering how she's dressed.

00:04:42.466 --> 00:04:43.966
And given that they're spending the entire

00:04:43.966 --> 00:04:47.933
night up there and likely experiencing
some intense wind chill from flying fast.

00:04:47.933 --> 00:04:49.616
They might be hot under the collar,

00:04:49.616 --> 00:04:52.100
but the rest of their bodies
are going to be ice cold.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.516
And sick,
they're going to be sick as well.

00:04:53.516 --> 00:04:55.066
Altitude sickness, to be exact.

00:04:55.066 --> 00:04:58.550
Between 5,000 and 10,000 feet in the air,
the air pressure is low enough

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:01.883
to cause headaches, nausea, fatigue,
dizziness and shortness of breath.

00:05:01.883 --> 00:05:04.200
This happens
because of a fall in barometric pressure,

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.583
which causes the tissue in your lungs
and brain to swell in an attempt

00:05:07.583 --> 00:05:08.700
to get more oxygen.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:11.266
That being said at this altitude,
while it would be unpleasant.

00:05:11.266 --> 00:05:12.950
It wouldn't outright kill them.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:16.216
Fun fact by the way, all of this is
actually why planes are pressurized.

00:05:16.216 --> 00:05:18.200
It keeps the pressure
the same as where you took off,

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.950
so the oxygen levels remain stable.

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:22.016
While also protecting you
from the colder temperatures

00:05:22.016 --> 00:05:23.850
at the much higher cruising altitude.

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.066
Okay,
so if the height’s going to make them

00:05:25.066 --> 00:05:27.616
chilly and woozy,
what about how fast they're flying?

00:05:27.616 --> 00:05:30.233
Well, to figure this one out, we're going
to need a few key bits of information.

00:05:30.233 --> 00:05:32.666
How far they traveled
and the timeframe they do it in.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.250
Let's start off with the distance,
shall we?

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:36.683
Obviously
the pair start off in the city of Agrabah.

00:05:36.683 --> 00:05:39.233
But Agrabah, it's
not exactly a real place.

00:05:39.233 --> 00:05:41.633
So how are we supposed to figure out where
we're going to be?

00:05:41.633 --> 00:05:43.250
Well, we've got ourselves a few options.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.750
Geographically we know that it's a city
in the middle of a desert,

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.766
but we also know it's close
to either a lake or large river.

00:05:48.766 --> 00:05:50.666
We know this thanks to a moment
in the middle of the movie

00:05:50.666 --> 00:05:53.183
when Aladdin is nearly drowned by Jafar’s
goons.

00:05:53.183 --> 00:05:55.433
Additionally, we have to remember that
the opening song is straight up

00:05:55.433 --> 00:05:59.216
called Arabian Nights,
implying that Agrabah is in Arabia,

00:05:59.216 --> 00:06:00.566
a very specific place.

00:06:00.566 --> 00:06:03.900
This peninsula in West Asia
between Africa and Southeast Asia.

00:06:04.016 --> 00:06:05.550
So where exactly are we?

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:08.700
Well, a lot of fans online assume
that Agrabah is located near the River

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:17.600
Jordan, because in the intro,
the merchant says this.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:18.900
However, when you actually break down

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:22.216
what he's saying here, he's not denoting
how close to the River Jordan they are,

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:26.033
only that Agrabah has the finest goods
on this side of the River Jordan.

00:06:26.033 --> 00:06:29.550
That could literally mean anywhere
to the east or the west of the river.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:31.550
You know, basically the entire planet.

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:34.583
Plus, in the Aladdin Animated Series,
though we do occasionally see

00:06:34.583 --> 00:06:38.450
a river in the show, it's never explicitly
called anything, let alone the Jordan.

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:40.850
So long story short, we're actually going
to need something else here.

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:42.300
Elsewhere in the opening song,
the merchant

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:46.050
says that he comes from a faraway place
where the caravan camels roam.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.450
Camel caravans
are actually very much a real thing,

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:51.233
most commonly found in the Saharan desert
of northern Africa.

00:06:51.266 --> 00:06:53.866
Though certain breeds of camels
were also used for this sort of travel

00:06:53.866 --> 00:06:57.116
and trade in the Middle East,
Central Asia, Mongolia and China.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.300
Again, not really helping us
narrow things down all that much.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:00.616
So what else could we look at?

00:07:00.616 --> 00:07:01.666
We could look at where

00:07:01.666 --> 00:07:04.816
the actual story of Aladdin originated,
which isn't where you'd expect.

00:07:04.816 --> 00:07:07.850
The original version of the tale
actually comes from China.

00:07:07.883 --> 00:07:09.866
Again,
not really working for our story here

00:07:09.866 --> 00:07:11.816
because this one's clearly
based on the Middle East.

00:07:11.816 --> 00:07:14.633
So then I thought, maybe we could use
the clothing of the characters

00:07:14.633 --> 00:07:17.100
and the architecture of the city
to try and pin something down.

00:07:17.116 --> 00:07:20.516
The architecture from Agrabah’s palace
clearly took inspiration from the Taj

00:07:20.516 --> 00:07:21.350
Mahal of India.

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:23.416
It's even located in a city named Agra.

00:07:23.416 --> 00:07:24.866
So I thought we might be
getting somewhere.

00:07:24.866 --> 00:07:27.983
But here's the thing, India, it’s
nowhere near the Arabian Peninsula.

00:07:27.983 --> 00:07:31.316
Arabian Nights are not happening there
in that subcontinent,

00:07:31.316 --> 00:07:32.616
so back to the drawing board.

00:07:32.616 --> 00:07:34.783
The clothing:
the clothing worn by characters

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.800
like Aladdin, Jasmine
and the Sultan resemble

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:37.366
what would have been

00:07:37.366 --> 00:07:41.266
worn by citizens of the Iraqi city,
Baghdad, though with a lot of artistic

00:07:41.266 --> 00:07:44.333
and cultural shortcuts
and inaccuracies thrown in by Disney.

00:07:44.333 --> 00:07:46.316
So that right
there, it’s a pretty strong lead

00:07:46.316 --> 00:07:48.750
that gets even stronger
once you consider this.

00:07:48.766 --> 00:07:50.850
According to John Musker,
co-director of the film,

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:54.116
the first treatment of the movie
was set in Baghdad, Iraq.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:55.816
However,
while the movie was in development,

00:07:55.816 --> 00:07:58.966
the first Gulf War broke out in the area,
and corporate executive Roy

00:07:58.966 --> 00:08:02.750
Disney insisted that Aladdin couldn't
be explicitly set in Baghdad.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:05.250
And thus Agrabah was created
as a stand in.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.800
And there is a bit of evidence
in the movie

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:09.416
for why this lines up with everything else
that we've talked about.

00:08:09.416 --> 00:08:11.183
Geographically, Baghdad lines up

00:08:11.183 --> 00:08:14.366
with what we see around Agrabah,
with the vast swaths of desert.

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:17.366
The city is built on the Tigris River,
which could be a stand in

00:08:17.366 --> 00:08:19.616
for all the bodies of water
that we see in the movie and the show.

00:08:19.616 --> 00:08:21.916
Baghdad was historically
one of the most important urban

00:08:21.916 --> 00:08:24.866
stops along the Silk Road,
which would have seen camel caravans

00:08:24.866 --> 00:08:25.966
stopping by frequently.

00:08:25.966 --> 00:08:27.600
It's also right on the edge of Arabia,

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:30.900
so it could be argued to be a part of it,
thus giving it Arabian Nights.

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:34.583
Additionally, in the Cave of Wonders,
you can spot this statue of Lamassu,

00:08:34.583 --> 00:08:38.716
an ancient Mesopotamian deity
which originated in Sumerian territory,

00:08:38.716 --> 00:08:41.750
very close to where modern day
Baghdad is located.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.166
Pretty much all the clues match,

00:08:43.166 --> 00:08:46.250
which means that we're going to be
using Baghdad as our stand in for Agrabah

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:47.400
for our purposes today.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:48.716
So now that we know roughly where

00:08:48.716 --> 00:08:51.566
Aladdin and Jasmine start their journey,
where do they actually go?

00:08:51.566 --> 00:08:53.983
Well, over the course of the song,
we see them fly through the pyramids

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.900
and past the Sphinx outside Cairo, Egypt,
then up to the Acropolis in Athens,

00:08:57.900 --> 00:08:59.750
Greece,
before completing their little song

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:01.816
at the Forbidden City in Beijing, China.

00:09:01.816 --> 00:09:04.133
It doesn't take a geographic genius
to see that that right there.

00:09:04.133 --> 00:09:06.150
That is a long journey.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:08.266
But just how long exactly is it?

00:09:08.266 --> 00:09:09.200
Well, let's break it down.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.283
Assuming that the carpet took the shortest
possible route between each stop on its

00:09:12.283 --> 00:09:17.600
journey, it's roughly 780 miles
or 1,260 kilometers from Baghdad to Cairo.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:18.016
The second

00:09:18.016 --> 00:09:22.666
leg from Cairo to Athens is a bit shorter,
700 miles or 1,120 kilometers.

00:09:22.666 --> 00:09:24.200
The most harrowing leg of the journey

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:27.233
would be from Athens to Beijing
so they could catch those fireworks,

00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:30.283
which is a staggering 4,730

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.866
miles or 7,600 kilometers.

00:09:33.466 --> 00:09:36.016
I just feel my legs
cramping up thinking about that flight.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:37.400
Finally flying from Beijing

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:40.433
back to Baghdad to get home in time
for the Sultan to not start a manhunt.

00:09:40.433 --> 00:09:42.950
It would be another painful 4,000 miles,

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:46.700
3,920 miles, to be specific, or 6,310
kilometers.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:48.266
Just in case you weren't keeping
track there.

00:09:48.266 --> 00:09:51.266
That means that during their little date
night, Aladdin and Jasmine flew

00:09:51.266 --> 00:09:57.650
a jaw dropping
10,130 miles or 16,300 kilometers.

00:09:57.650 --> 00:09:59.516
That is a lot.

00:09:59.516 --> 00:10:03.900
If you did this on a normal commercial
flight, it would take you over 20 hours.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:05.416
The longest normally operated

00:10:05.416 --> 00:10:08.716
nonstop flight in the world
flies between Singapore and New York City.

00:10:08.716 --> 00:10:13.033
That one clocks in at just over
9,500 miles or 15,300

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:16.966
kilometers
and takes nearly 19 agonizing hours.

00:10:16.966 --> 00:10:20.483
So now that we know how far they flew,
how fast were they going there?

00:10:20.483 --> 00:10:23.966
Since Aladdin gets Jasmine back to Agrabah
before any sorts of alarms of missing

00:10:23.966 --> 00:10:27.733
princess are raised, this absolutely
would not have taken the 20 plus hours

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:29.183
that it would take a modern airplane.

00:10:29.183 --> 00:10:30.833
In fact,
when I started researching this theory,

00:10:30.833 --> 00:10:32.516
I actually wondered
if it was going to be possible

00:10:32.516 --> 00:10:35.400
for all of these locations
to be nighttime at the same time.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:38.400
But considering that Beijing
is the only real outlier here,

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:42.683
just 5 hours ahead of Baghdad,
Cairo and Athens, it should be possible.

00:10:42.683 --> 00:10:45.200
But that does beg a bit of a bigger
question here.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.416
Sure, it's possible for all these places
to be night at the same time.

00:10:48.416 --> 00:10:51.733
But how long do Aladdin
and Jasmine actually have to fly this far?

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:55.133
When Aladdin gets to Jasmine's window,
it's already dark out with the stars

00:10:55.133 --> 00:10:58.583
clearly visible in the night sky,
which puts it decidedly after sunset.

00:10:58.583 --> 00:11:00.016
And they still need to catch the fireworks

00:11:00.016 --> 00:11:02.300
over in Beijing
before heading back to Agrabah.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.766
So when are those fireworks
possibly happening?

00:11:04.766 --> 00:11:07.816
Now, sadly, I have to admit,
I do not have 1,000 year old fireworks

00:11:07.816 --> 00:11:10.166
schedule from Beijing to double
check the time here.

00:11:10.166 --> 00:11:12.166
But you know what? We're going to make
a pretty reasonable estimate.

00:11:12.166 --> 00:11:13.950
First off, we're going to assume
that this is happening

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:16.183
on the Chinese New Year
for a couple of reasons.

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:18.233
During this scene,
we see a dancing dragon,

00:11:18.233 --> 00:11:21.316
which is a traditional Chinese
puppet used during celebrations.

00:11:21.316 --> 00:11:23.850
The large, impressive display of fireworks
also tells us

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:27.050
that this is some sort of a festival
and this is important because fireworks

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:28.050
during the Chinese New Year

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:30.650
can last into the wee
hours of the morning, giving Aladdin

00:11:30.650 --> 00:11:33.766
and Jasmine the most possible
time to leave Baghdad, Agrabah, pass

00:11:33.766 --> 00:11:36.200
by the Pyramids and Acropolis
and then head on over to Beijing

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:37.783
to watch the fireworks on this building.

00:11:37.783 --> 00:11:39.800
That right there.
That's the Forbidden City,

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:42.166
an imperial palace
at the center of the city of Beijing.

00:11:42.166 --> 00:11:45.233
Of all the landmarks that they visit,
this one was actually the last

00:11:45.233 --> 00:11:47.900
to be constructed,
completed in the year 1420.

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:50.216
So using that,
we know that at the earliest

00:11:50.216 --> 00:11:52.666
this movie can take
place is the year 1420.

00:11:52.666 --> 00:11:53.716
And just to keep things simple,

00:11:53.716 --> 00:11:55.850
we're going to be using
that as our new year here.

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:57.766
The Chinese New Year is a festival
that celebrates

00:11:57.766 --> 00:12:00.466
the beginning of a new year
on the traditional Chinese calendar,

00:12:00.466 --> 00:12:03.650
which usually falls on the second new moon
after the winter solstice.

00:12:03.650 --> 00:12:07.666
In the year 1420, the Chinese New Year
began on January 24th,

00:12:07.666 --> 00:12:10.850
and according to the National Oceanic
and Atmospheric Administration,

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:15.266
the sun set in Baghdad
that day at approximately 5:22 p.m.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:17.750
Let's just make it an even 5:30
to keep it nice.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:20.833
In modern day China, during festivals
like the Chinese New Year, festivals

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:24.150
can be set off continuously
for up to 2 hours after midnight,

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:26.033
so that right
there gives us our flight cut off.

00:12:26.033 --> 00:12:28.016
We are getting to Beijing by 2 a.m.

00:12:28.016 --> 00:12:29.116
at the latest.

00:12:29.116 --> 00:12:30.166
Using what we found out

00:12:30.166 --> 00:12:33.000
earlier about flight distances,
if you were to board a commercial flight

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:34.200
from Baghdad to Cairo

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:37.966
to Athens to Beijing, that would normally
take over 12 hours to fly.

00:12:37.966 --> 00:12:40.033
And that's not even considering the fact
that they need to be back

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:41.333
and Agrabah by the morning.

00:12:41.333 --> 00:12:43.766
But since Beijing is 5 hours
ahead of Baghdad,

00:12:43.766 --> 00:12:46.050
that puts the time there at 10:30,

00:12:46.066 --> 00:12:50.383
meaning that Aladdin and Jasmine
only have roughly three and a half hours

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:53.416
to travel the 6,000
plus miles between all their stops

00:12:53.416 --> 00:12:56.250
before that fireworks
display ends in Beijing.

00:12:56.266 --> 00:13:01.100
So to make it,
they need to be traveling just about 1,775

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:04.950
miles an hour
or nearly 3,000 kilometers an hour.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:08.333
That is more than twice
the speed of sound, which opens up

00:13:08.333 --> 00:13:11.383
a massive can of worms
because moving faster than Mach 2?

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:12.533
That is no joke.

00:13:12.533 --> 00:13:15.266
They're going to be subjected
to some crazy forces.

00:13:15.266 --> 00:13:18.916
Using this drag equation and the fact
that Disney mandates their Aladdins in the

00:13:18.916 --> 00:13:23.216
theme parks to be between a height of 5
foot 10 and 6 foot, we can calculate that

00:13:23.216 --> 00:13:27.883
Aladdin and Jasmine are both facing
roughly 144,000

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:31.466
Newtons of force every single second
that they're flying on that carpet.

00:13:31.466 --> 00:13:34.666
To put that insane amount of force
into perspective, an average person

00:13:34.666 --> 00:13:40.250
experiences about 67,000 Newtons of force
in a 40 mile per hour car collision.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:41.450
And that's just one quick hit.

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:44.000
Not every single second
that they're in the air.

00:13:44.033 --> 00:13:47.250
The strongest bone in the human body
is the femur, your thigh bone.

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:50.716
And snapping a femur only takes
about 4,000 Newtons of direct pressure.

00:13:50.716 --> 00:13:51.766
During this date, Aladdin

00:13:51.766 --> 00:13:56.150
forced him and Jasmine to experience
more than 36 times that amount of force.

00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:56.783
I actually wondered

00:13:56.783 --> 00:14:00.150
if this would be powerful enough
to rip the skin clean off their bones.

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.750
But running those numbers
against the tensile strength of skin meant

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:06.016
that you needed something closer
to 10 million Newtons to make it happen.

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:08.333
It would still be enough
to break their bodies and send Aladdin

00:14:08.333 --> 00:14:14.850
and Jasmine hurtling off the carpet,
falling to the ground below.

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:16.050
Yeah, you can say that again.

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:18.150
And if they're lucky,
the pain from snapping all their bones

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:20.866
would cause them to pass out
before they hit the ground and died.

00:14:20.866 --> 00:14:21.650
It's pretty dark.

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:22.466
And definitely not

00:14:22.466 --> 00:14:25.700
what Disney wants us to imagine
happening to their beloved characters.

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:28.916
But here's the thing, this isn't
the only incarnation of these characters

00:14:28.916 --> 00:14:31.966
to exist within the massive canon
of the Disney Cinematic Universe.

00:14:31.966 --> 00:14:33.200
In fact, there's another

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:37.216
official version of this tragic
carpet ride in the live action remake.

00:14:37.216 --> 00:14:39.266
If you don't remember this thing,
I mean, fair.

00:14:39.266 --> 00:14:40.200
But the long and short of it

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:43.850
is that this new version doesn't quite
put the ‘world’ into a Whole New World.

00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:45.266
They don't fly across continents,

00:14:45.266 --> 00:14:48.500
they don't visit the Pyramids
or the Acropolis or the Forbidden City.

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:50.266
Instead, everything
from this musical number

00:14:50.266 --> 00:14:52.700
in the new movie
are things that you could feasibly find in

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:55.950
and around the immediate area of Baghdad
during this time period.

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:58.800
You have palm trees, elephants,
mountains, rivers, deserts.

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:01.800
This version of Aladdin and Jasmine
aren't flying thousands of miles,

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:05.483
giving the princess a new lease on life
and sparking a globe trotting romance.

00:15:05.483 --> 00:15:09.600
It all just feels very small, very real,
not very magical.

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:12.750
And there, I think, is the lesson
that we can take away from all of this.

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:15.200
Scientifically speaking, yes,
this remake handles

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:18.450
A Whole New World way more realistically
than the animated version did.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:21.883
But in doing so, it's really a slap
to the face of what this moment

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:22.816
meant to the story.

00:15:22.816 --> 00:15:24.950
It took all the fun and whimsy
out of this journey.

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:28.433
It took away the magic, and instead
it turned it into something boring.

00:15:28.433 --> 00:15:31.633
And even though I'm a man of science,
at the end of the day, sometimes

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:33.766
you really need that bit of magic.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:34.616
But hey!

00:15:34.616 --> 00:15:38.033
If you want another Aladdin theory
right now, why not check out our video

00:15:38.033 --> 00:15:39.016
where we tell Aladdin

00:15:39.016 --> 00:15:42.716
exactly how to get Jasmine to marry him
in just a single wish?

00:15:42.716 --> 00:15:45.166
Or if you want to know how horrifying
another Disney

00:15:45.166 --> 00:15:47.600
Renaissance classic would be
if it were real, check out our theory

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:50.966
where we see what a real life
Little Mermaid would actually look like.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.533
Spoiler alert,
you will not want to kiss da girl.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:56.366
And as always, remember,
my friends, it's all just a theory.

00:15:56.366 --> 00:15:59.950
A FILM THEORY! Aaaaaaand cut.

